{\b\fs28 University of Toronto \endash  Classics}\par
\par
{\b George Boys-Stones  |  University of Toronto (Classics)}\par
george.boysstones@utoronto.ca\par
{\b Subject:} ManuscriptDB: a geographic, bilingual platform for ancient manuscripts\par
\par
Dear Professor Boys-Stones,\par
\par
My name is Ethan Gill, and I am an MA student in the Department for the Study of Religion at the University of Toronto. Over the past while I have been building ManuscriptDB, a web platform that organizes ancient manuscripts geographically, plotting each one on an interactive map, and presenting them in both the original language and an English translation within a single, user-friendly interface.\par
\par
Given your work on ancient philosophy, Platonism, and ancient ethics, I thought this project might be of particular interest to you.\par
\par
I am hoping ManuscriptDB can be a useful resource for undergraduates, graduate students, and faculty alike. If you have any spare time and interest, I would be grateful if you explored the interface and shared any feedback or features you would like to see. You can find it at ManuscriptDB.org.\par
\par
Thank you for your time and support.\par
\par
Best regards,\par
Ethan Gill\par
MA Student, Department for the Study of Religion, University of Toronto\par
